  "uncertainty_note": "Bands and errors are the plotted values. See the figure caption for confidence level and estimator.",
  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "\\textbf{The endpoint response retains the history of feedback.} {Three-spin weak-end chain. Feedback on spin 2 is activated at $\\omega_ct=10$ (a,c) or stopped at $20$ or $30$ (b,d), compared with never/always controls.} Colour-matched vertical dashed guides mark the changes; each column's legend applies to both panels in that column. The upper row shows signed $G_{13}^{zz}$ and the lower row the concurrence of the averaged endpoint state. The full joint state is retained through each switch. Solid curves and pointwise 95\\% bands are checked HOPS estimates; same-colour dotted curves are master equations. The delayed-on record ends at $40$, and the stop comparisons extend to $80$. Preparation, loss profile and controller match Fig.~\\ref{fig:feedback3}."
}
